{{short description|Chronology of mathematics}}
{{Use mdy dates|date=November 2026}}

This is a [[timeline]] of [[pure mathematics|pure]] and [[applied mathematics]] [[History of mathematics|history]]. It is divided into three stages, corresponding to stages in the [[History of mathematical notation|development of mathematical notation]]: a "rhetorical" stage in which calculations are described purely by words, a "syncopated" stage in which quantities and common algebraic operations are beginning to be represented by symbolic abbreviations, and finally a "symbolic" stage, in which comprehensive notational systems for formulas are the norm. Below the timeline, the same events are grouped by civilization, as in [[History of mathematics]].

